=== what rung 6 does not carry over from APL ===

SKIP  prod ← ∘.×  out of scope: a derived function as a VALUE is a tacit definition; only `+.×` is a member of AplFnD, and only so that `+.×⍤2⊢` parses (rung 7)
SKIP  f.g with an array operand  out of scope: `⌷` and the eight direct outer glyphs are the only new members of the glyph tables; a NUMBER as an operand of ∘. or . has no rule
SKIP  ∘.g on matrices  out of scope: the outer product is declared over rank 0 and rank 1 only, which is every shape the chapter and the two programs use
SKIP  f.g over rank 3  out of scope: only through ⍤2, which is how the program writes it (Z2-Z4); there is no rank-3 overload of aplMatMul itself
SKIP  ⍤0 1 with a matrix left argument  out of scope: the left cells are scalars by construction, so the left argument is a scalar or a vector
SKIP  A +.× A  out of scope: a mismatched product is APL's LENGTH ERROR, a catchable contract violation; the shipped DOT's own shared nat catches it too, but as a ProgramError no catch clause takes (w01_dot.out.0)
